    "debrief":  {
                    "realTeam":  "In 2009 the rover Spirit got stuck in soft soil and could not turn its solar panels toward the low winter Sun. As the Mars winter came, its power kept dropping and it went into a deep sleep to save energy. Spirit sent its last message on March 22, 2010. The team listened for more than a year and ended the mission in May 2011.",
                    "tryNext":  "Switch off the Science lab and the Radio on the very first sol. Saving power early is what gets you through winter.",
                    "realScience":  {
                                        "title":  "Why winter is hard for solar power",
                                        "text":  "In winter the Sun stays low in the sky, so its light hits the panels at a slant and makes less power. The nights are colder too, so heaters need more energy. Spirit was stuck at a bad angle, tilted away from the Sun, which made winter even harder.",
                                        "glossary":  "solar"
                                    },
                    "sources":  [
                                    "mer_historynasa_images"
                                ]
                },
